Record the CSS transitions/animations resolve_stylist finishes (Roves).

Stylo's restyle removes a finished transition from its ElementAnimationSet in
the same traversal that follows Blitz's Running -> Finished step, so an embedder
reading BaseDocument::animations() afterwards sees it disappear exactly like a
canceled one (Element.getAnimations then rejected `finished` with AbortError,
CI 43047120469). This captures every entry the state machine moves to Finished,
before the traversal, and lets the embedder take them. Nothing in Blitz's own
behavior changes; at most FINISHED_ANIMATIONS_CAP records are kept.

Base: crates.io blitz-dom 0.3.0-beta.4 + 0001. Applied in
support/blitz-v8-probe/vendor/blitz-dom; see ROVES_PATCHES.md there.

